                            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived stack
                  %h2#theorems Theorems
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barr%27s+theorem"} Barr's theorem
                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/topos+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_localization"} Relation to localization
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#factorizations_and_images"} Factorizations and images
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong geometric embedding
            is the right notion of embedding or inclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topoi"} topoi
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \hookrightarrow E
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtoposes"} subtoposes
          %p
            Notably the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(S) \hookrightarrow PSh(S)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            into its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            or more generally the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mi E
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_j E \hookrightarrow E
            of sheaves in a topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            itself, is a geometric embedding. Actually every geometric embedding is of this form, up to equivalence of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topoi
          %p
            Another perspective is that a geometric embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \hookrightarrow E
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            at the class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            or morphisms that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to F
            sends to isomorphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            The induced geometric morphism of a topological immersion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \hookrightarrow Y
            is a geometric embedding. The converse holds if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            space. (Example A4.2.12(c) in (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone
            ))
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            two
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topoi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi E
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi F
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F \stackrel{f}{\to}
                  E
                  \\;\;\;\;
                  F \stackrel{\stackrel{f_*}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{f^*}{\longleftarrow}} E
          %p
            is a
            %strong geometric embedding
            if the following equivalent conditions are satisfied
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
                functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
                (so that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is a full
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
                of
                = succeed ");" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %li
              %p
                the counit
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Id
                        %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon :  f^* f_* \to Id_{F}
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjunction
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^* \dashv f_*)
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %li
              %p
                there is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topology
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                and an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo :
                      %mi F
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mi j
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e : F \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Sh_j E
                such that the diagram of geometric morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi F
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mi E
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mi e
                              %msup
                                %mo ↘
                                %mo ≃
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                                %mi i
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Sh
                                %mi j
                              %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{ F &amp;\stackrel{f_*}{\to}&amp; E \\ &amp; {}_{e}\searrow^\simeq &amp; \uparrow^{i} \\ &amp;&amp; Sh_j E}
                commutes up to natural isomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^* i^* \simeq f^*
          %p
            That the first two conditions are equivalent is standard, that the third one is equivalent to the first two is for instance corollary 7 in section VII, 4 of (
            %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"}> MacLaneMoerdijk
            )
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_localization Relation to localization
          %p
            There is a close relation between geometric embedding and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : F \hookrightarrow E
            be a geometric embedding and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \subset Mor(E)
            be the class of morphisms sent by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            to isomorphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p We have:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is equivalent to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi W
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E[W]^{-1}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is equivalent to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  on
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
          %p
            This fact connects for instance the description of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
            in terms of geometric embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(S) \hookrightarrow PSh(S)
            as described for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              MacLane-Moerdijk,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
          %p
            with that in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphisms"} local isomorphisms
          %ul
            %li
              Kashiwara-Schapira,
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} Categories and Sheaves
          %p
            Moreover, this is the basis on which sheafification is generalized to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheafification"} (∞,1)-sheafification
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
              \.
          %p The following gives a detailed proof of the above assertion.
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : Id_E \to f_* f^*
            for the unit of the adjunction.
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
            is fully faithful we will identify objects and morphism of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            with their images in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar {(-)} := f^*
            for the left adjoint.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              for the class of morphism that are sent to isomorphism under
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi c
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W = (f^*)^{-1}\{g: c\stackrel{\simeq}{\to} d \in Mor(E)\}
                    \\,.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              equipped with the class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              satisfies 2-out-of-3.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p Follows since isomorphisms satisfy 2-out-of-3.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              is a left
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} multiplicative system
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              This follows using the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
              is left exact and hence preserves finite limits.
            %p In more detail:
            %p We have already seen in the previous proposition that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  every isomorphism is in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  is closed under composition.
            %p It remains to check the following points:
            %p Given any
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi w
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi b
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi h
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; a
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^w
                    \\\
                    b &amp;\stackrel{h}{\to}&amp; c
                    }
            %p
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in W
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %mi w
                                %mo ′
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi w
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi b
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi h
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    d &amp;\to&amp; a
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{w'} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^w
                    \\\
                    b &amp;\stackrel{h}{\to}&amp; c
                    }
            %p
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w' \in W
            %p
              To get this, take this to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              diagram,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ′
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi h
                        %mo *
                      %mi w
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w' := h^* w
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
              preserves pullbacks, it follows that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi d
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %mover
                                  %mi w
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                                %mo ′
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mover
                                %mi w
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi b
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mover
                                %mi h
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\bar d &amp;\to&amp; \bar a
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\bar w'} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\bar w}
                    \\\
                    \\bar b &amp;\stackrel{\bar h}{\to}&amp; \bar c
                    }
            %p
              is a pullback diagram in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi w
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo ′
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi h
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mi w
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar w' = \bar h^* \bar w
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi w
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar w
              is an isomorphism. Therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi w
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar w'
              is an isomorphism, therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w'
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %p Finally for every
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi s
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi r
                    %mi b
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi w
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a \stackrel{\stackrel{r}{\to}}{\stackrel{s}{\to}} b \stackrel{w}{\to} c
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in W
              such that the two composites coincide, we need to find
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                        %mo ′
                    %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi s
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi r
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d \stackrel{w'}{\to} a \stackrel{\stackrel{r}{\to}}{\stackrel{s}{\to}} b
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w' \in W
              such that the composites again coincide.
            %p
              To get this, take
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w'
              to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
              of the two morphisms. Sending everything with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              we find from
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi r
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi b
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi w
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar a \stackrel{\stackrel{\bar r}{\to}}{\stackrel{\bar s}{\to}} b \stackrel{\bar w}{\to} c
            %p
              that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo =
                      %mover
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar r = \bar s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi w
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar w
              is an isomorphism. This implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi w
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar w'
              is the equalizer
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mo ′
                    %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi r
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar d \stackrel{\bar w'}{\to} a \stackrel{\stackrel{\bar r}{\to}}{\stackrel{\bar s}{\to}} b
            %p
              of two equal morphism, hence an identity. So
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w'
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in E
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the unit
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi a
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_a : a \to \bar a
                  is in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                  is already in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  then the unit is already an isomorphism.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              This follows from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+identities"} triangle identities
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mi Id
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;
                    \\nearrow &amp;\Downarrow^{\eta}&amp; \searrow^{Id_E}
                    \\\
                    E
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\bar{(-)}}{\to}&amp;
                    F
                    \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                    E
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\bar{(-)}}{\to}&amp;
                    F
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp;
                    \\searrow &amp;\Downarrow^{\simeq}&amp; \nearrow_{Id_F}
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \=
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    \&amp; \nearrow \searrow^{\bar{(-)}}
                    \\\
                    E
                    \&amp;\Downarrow^{Id}&amp;
                    F
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow \nearrow_{\bar{(-)}}
                    }
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mi Id
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                            %mo ↗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp;
                    \\nearrow &amp;\Downarrow^{\eta}&amp; \searrow^{Id_E}
                    \\\
                    F
                    \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                    E
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\bar{(-)}}{\to}&amp;
                    F
                    \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                    E
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    \\searrow &amp;\Downarrow^{\simeq}&amp; \nearrow_{Id_F}
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \=
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    \&amp; \nearrow \searrow
                    \\\
                    F
                    \&amp;\Downarrow^{Id}&amp;
                    E
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow \nearrow
                    }
            %p In components they say that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for every
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in E
                  we have
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mover
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi η
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                              %mi a
                        %mover
                          %mover
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ≃
                        %mover
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi Id
                          %mover
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\bar a \stackrel{\bar \eta_a}{\to} \bar{\bar a} \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \bar a) = Id_{\bar a}
              %li
                %p
                  for every
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in F
                  we have
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi a
                        %mover
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ≃
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi Id
                          %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a \stackrel{\eta_a}{\to} \bar a \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} a)  = Id_a
            %p This implies the claim.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in E
              is
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
              if for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi c
                    %mo →
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : c \to d
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              the map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g^* : Hom_E(d,a) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    Hom_E(c,a)
            %p obtained by precomposition is an isomorphism.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Up to isomorphism, the
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              First assume that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is
              = succeed "-local." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %p
              Notice that the existence of the required isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_F(d,a) \simeq Hom_F(c,a)
              is equivalent to the statement that for every diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi h
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; d
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{h}
                    \\\
                    a
                    }
            %p there is a unique extension
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi h
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; d
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{h} &amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    a
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              To see the existence of this extension, hit the original diagram with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
              to get
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi d
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mover
                                %mi h
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\bar c &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; \bar d
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\bar h}
                    \\\
                    \\bar a \simeq a
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo →
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \to d
              is in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar c \to \bar d
              here is an isomorphism. By the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is already in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar a \simeq a
              since the counit is an isomorphism. Therefore this diagram clearly has a unique extension
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi d
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mover
                                %mi h
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∃
                                %mo !
                                %mi k
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\bar c &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; \bar d
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\bar h} &amp; \swarrow_{\exists ! k}
                    \\\
                    \\bar a \simeq a
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the hom-isomorphism (using full faithfullness of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
              to work entirely in
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_E(\bar d, a) \simeq Hom_E(d,a)
            %p
              this defines a morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo :
                      %mi d
                      %mo →
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k : d \to a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              through the naturality diagram of the hom-isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mover
                              %mi d
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mo ,
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo ,
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mover
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mo ,
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Hom_E(\bar d, \bar a) &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; Hom_E(d,\bar a)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    Hom_E(\bar c, \bar a) &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; Hom_E(c,\bar a)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k : d \to a
              does extend the original diagram. Again by the Hom-isomorphism, it is the unique morphism with this property.
            %p
              So
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in F
              is
              = succeed "-local." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %p
              Now for the converse, assume that a given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is
              = succeed "-local." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %p
              By one of the above propositions we know that the unit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_a : a \to \bar a
              is in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              = succeed "-locality" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              it follows that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    a &amp;\stackrel{\eta_a}{\to}&amp; \bar a
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{Id_a}
                    \\\
                    a
                    }
            %p has an extension
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    a &amp;\stackrel{\eta_a}{\to}&amp; \bar a
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{Id_a} &amp; \swarrow_{\rho_a}
                    \\\
                    a
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the 2-out-of-3 property of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              shown in one of the above propositions, (using that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Id
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_a
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo →
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_a : \bar a \to a
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar a
              is in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              and therefore
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mover
                                    %mi a
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\bar a &amp;\stackrel{\rho_a}{\to}&amp; a
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{Id_{\bar a}}
                    \\\
                    \\bar a
                    }
            %p has an extension
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mover
                                    %mi a
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi λ
                                  %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\bar a &amp;\stackrel{\rho_a}{\to}&amp; a
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{Id_{\bar a}} &amp; \swarrow_{\lambda_a}
                    \\\
                    \\bar a
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              So
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_a
              has a left inverse
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_a
              which itself has a left inverse
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_a
              is also a right inverse to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_a
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mi a
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mi a
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi a
                            %munder
                              %munder
                                %mrow
                                  %mover
                                    %mo →
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi ρ
                                        %mi a
                                  %mover
                                    %mo →
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi λ
                                        %mi a
                                %mo ⏟
                              %mi id
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mi a
                            %munder
                              %munder
                                %mrow
                                  %mover
                                    %mo →
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi η
                                        %mi a
                                  %mover
                                    %mo →
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi ρ
                                        %mi a
                                %mo ⏟
                              %mi id
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi λ
                                  %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mi a
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi λ
                                  %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Id
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\stackrel{\rho_a}{\to}
                    \\stackrel{\eta_a}{\to}
                    \&amp; =
                    \\stackrel{\rho_a}{\to}
                    \\stackrel{\eta_a}{\to}
                    \\underset{id}{\underbrace{
                    \\stackrel{\rho_a}{\to}
                    \\stackrel{\lambda_a}{\to}
                    }}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\stackrel{\rho_a}{\to}
                    \\underset{id}{\underbrace{
                    \\stackrel{\eta_a}{\to}
                    \\stackrel{\rho_a}{\to}
                    }}
                    \\stackrel{\lambda_a}{\to}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=
                    \\stackrel{\rho_a}{\to}
                    \\stackrel{\lambda_a}{\to}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=
                    Id
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              So if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_a : a \to \bar a
              is an isomorphism, hence that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is isomorphic to an object of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          .un_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is equivalent to the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo −
                        %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{W-loc}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              on
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              By standard reasoning (e.g.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} KS lemma 1.3.11
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo −
                        %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to E_{W-loc}
              and a natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mrow
                                %mi W
                                %mo −
                                %mi loc
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    F &amp;&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;&amp; E
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;\Downarrow^{\simeq}&amp; \nearrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; E_{W-loc}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \hookrightarrow E
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo −
                        %mi loc
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{W-loc} \hookrightarrow E
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                          %mo −
                          %mi loc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to E_{W-loc}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                          %mo −
                          %mi loc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \simeq E_{W-loc}
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E[W^{-1}]
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              By one of the above propositions we know that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} left multiplicative systems
            %p
              This implies that the localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E[W^{-1}]
              is (equivalent to) the category with the same objects as
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mi colim
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ′
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi W
                        %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{E[W^{-1}]}(a,b)
                    \=
                    \\underset{a' \stackrel{p \in W}{\to}a}{colim} Hom_E(a',b)
                    \\,.
            %p There is an obvious candidate for a functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F \to E[W^{-1}]
            %p
              given on objects by the usual embedding by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
              and on morphism by the map which regards a morphism trivially as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
              with left leg the identity
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi a
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mi b
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Id
                                    %mi a
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi a
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (a \to b)
                    \\;\;
                    \\mapsto
                    \\;\;
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    a &amp;\to&amp; b
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{Id_a}
                    \\\
                    a
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              For this to be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
              we need to show that this is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            %p
              To see essential surjectivity, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              be any object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_a : a \to \bar a
              be the component of the unit of our adjunction on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_a
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    a &amp;\stackrel{Id_a}{\to}&amp; a
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\eta_a}
                    \\\
                    \\bar a
                    }
            %p
              represents an element in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi W
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{E[W^{-1}]}(\bar a,a)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    a &amp;\stackrel{\eta_a}{\to}&amp; \bar a
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{Id_a}
                    \\\
                    a
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar a
              is in the image of our functor, this shows that it is essentially surjective.
            %p
              To see fullness and faithfulness, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, b\in F
              be any two objects. By one of the above propositions this means in particular that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi b
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi w
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    a' &amp;\to&amp; b
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^w
                    \\\
                    a
                    }
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in W
              has a unique extension
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi b
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi w
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    a' &amp;\to&amp; b
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^w &amp; \nearrow
                    \\\
                    a
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              But this implies that in the colimit that defines the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E[W^{-1}]
              all these spans are identified with spans whose left leg is the identiy. And these are clearly in bijection with the morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_E(a,b) \simeq Hom_F(a,b)
              so that indeed
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{E[W^{-1}]}(a,b)
                    \\simeq
                    Hom_{F}(a,b)
            %p
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b \in F
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} E[W^{-1}]
                    \\,.
          %h3#factorizations_and_images Factorizations and images
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+system+on+a+2-category"} factorization system
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
            whose left class is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+geometric+morphisms"} surjective geometric morphisms
            and whose right class is the geometric embeddings. The factorization of a geometric morphism can be said to construct its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            in the topos-theoretic sense.
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+surjection%2Fembedding+factorization"} geometric surjection/embedding factorization
          %p
            Moreover, each geometric embedding itself has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28dense%2Cclosed%29-factorization"} (dense,closed)-factorization
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %p
            In the more general context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (∞,1)-topos theory
            an
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-geometric embedding
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-geometric+morphism"} (∞,1)-geometric morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒳
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo ←
                  %mi 𝒴
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (f^* \dashv f_*) : \mathcal{X} \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\hookrightarrow}
                  \\mathcal{Y}
          %p
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} full and faithful (∞,1)-functor
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-category
            for more details.
          %h2#references References
          %p Section VII, 4 of
          %ul#MacLaneMoerdijk
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+Mac+Lane"} Saunders Mac Lane
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
          %p and section A4.2 of
          %ul#Johnstone
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Sketches of an elephant: a topos theory compendium
